  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from the date of this decision.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended by Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications: Site Location Plan, Reasonable Exception Statement � received 1st April 2025, 101 Rev. C, 102 Rev. C � received 19th May 2025\r\nReason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building, unless otherwise shown on the approved plans.\r\nReason: In order to safeguard the appearance of the area.",
    "Condition : 4 - Either side of the vehicle access hereby approved, visibility splay areas (the depth measured from the back of the footway and the widths outwards from the edges of the access, with a splay of at least 2.4 metres x 2.4 metres) shall be provided before the access and parking area is brought into use.  These areas shall be kept clear of any obstructions to visibility greater than 600 mm in height, including shrubs, planting, boundary walls, fences, gates, other means of enclosure or other structures or objects at all times.\r\nReason:  To ensure adequate visibility for drivers entering and leaving the site in the interests of pedestrian and vehicle safety.",
    "Condition : 5 - Prior to first use of the vehicle crossover hereby permitted the boundary wall shown on the plans shall have been erected in its entirety and shall thereafter be retained as such. \r\nReason - In the interests of highway and pedestrian safety together with the character of the area"
  ],
